<article class="article-wrap">
  <div class="article-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="article-tag">Guide</div>
      <h1>WhatsApp Business App vs. WhatsApp Business API: What is the Difference?</h1>
      <div class="article-meta"><span>Jun 19, 2026</span><span>·</span><span>5 min read</span></div>
      <p class="article-intro">Choosing the wrong WhatsApp product can limit your business scaling. Here is a detailed comparison of the free WhatsApp Business App and the enterprise-ready WhatsApp Business API.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="callout"><strong>Summary:</strong> Use the free <strong>Business App</strong> if you are a local shop or a freelancer. Upgrade to the <strong>Business API</strong> if you have a team, need automated CRM integrations, or want to send broadcasts to thousands of users daily.</div>

      <h2>WhatsApp Business App: The basics</h2>
      <p>The WhatsApp Business App is a free, standalone mobile app designed for small businesses. It looks and operates similarly to the personal WhatsApp app but includes basic business tools such as a business profile, product catalog, quick replies, away messages, and labels to organize chats.</p>
      <p><strong>Limits:</strong> You can only log in on up to 5 devices (4 browser windows + 1 phone). Additionally, broadcast lists are limited to exactly 256 contacts, and messages are only delivered if the recipient has saved your number in their address book.</p>

      <h2>WhatsApp Business API: The enterprise solution</h2>
      <p>The WhatsApp Business API (also known as the Cloud API) has no default user interface. Instead, you connect it to CRM software or customer support platforms like Hubspot, Zendesk, or custom AI engines. It is designed for medium to large enterprises that require robust, team-wide communication tools.</p>
      <p><strong>Benefits:</strong> Supports unlimited agents and devices. There is no contact saving requirement for broadcasts, meaning you can reach anyone. It allows complete integration with AI chatbots, supports message templates with interactive buttons, and enables the verified Green Tick badge next to your company name.</p>

      <h2>Comparison table</h2>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>Feature</th>
          <th>Business App</th>
          <th>Business API</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cost</td>
          <td>100% Free</td>
          <td>Paid per conversation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Devices</td>
          <td>Max 5 devices</td>
          <td>Unlimited agents</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Broadcast Limit</td>
          <td>256 per list</td>
          <td>Unlimited (Tiered)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Automation</td>
          <td>Basic auto-replies</td>
          <td>Advanced bots & APIs</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Green Tick</td>
          <td>Not available</td>
          <td>Available (Application needed)</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <h2>How to make your choice</h2>
      <p>If you are a solopreneur or a small local team handling under 50 inquiries a day, the free WhatsApp Business App is perfect. However, if your sales pipeline is expanding, you are running Meta Ads, or you want to connect AI qualification agents, you must migrate to the WhatsApp Business API. You can register for the API via Meta's developer dashboard or through business solution providers (BSPs).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="article-cta">
      <h3>Create links that work on both platforms</h3>
